### Outbound report to Odoo (on the "ringing" state change)
# Send from the 3CX Call Control API / webhook as soon as the outgoing call rings.
# event must be one of: ringing | answered | busy | noanswer.
# Do NOT send "failed"/"instant" -> deliberately creates no sticky mapping.

POST https://CHANGE-ME.odoo.example.com/api/3cx/outbound
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: CHANGE-ME
# X-Signature: <hex(hmac_sha256(body, SigningSecret))>   # only if a secret is set

{
  "event": "ringing",
  "extension": "105",
  "number": "+491701234567",
  "call_id": "abc-123"
}

### Inbound lookup (reference – in the CFD via Make HTTP Request)
POST https://CHANGE-ME.odoo.example.com/api/3cx/callback-routing
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: CHANGE-ME

{ "callerid": "+491701234567", "did": "089123456", "queue": "PROJECTS" }

### Presence (optional)
POST https://CHANGE-ME.odoo.example.com/api/3cx/presence
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: CHANGE-ME

{ "extension": "105", "state": "available", "registered": true }
